    "body":  "Closes #825\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\nAdds the official **PagerDuty** service connector to Switch\u0027s service connections catalog (`core/switch_core/connections/catalog/pagerduty/`):\n\n- **API Key Adapter Configuration**:\n  - Configures `adapter: api_key` with API key credential input.\n  - Multi-region choices (`pagerduty.com` for US and `eu.pagerduty.com` for EU) templating directly into the REST identity endpoint and MCP server URL.\n- **Identity Resolution**:\n  - Resolves identity via `GET https://api.{region}/users/me` with header `Authorization: Token token={api_key}`.\n  - Resolves account identity via `user.id` and label via `user.email`.\n- **MCP Server \u0026 Token Security**:\n  - Connects to hosted MCP endpoint (`https://mcp.{region}/mcp`) passing the key via `Authorization: Token token={api_key}`.\n  - Follows security requirements: `token: { kind: pass_through, max_lifetime: null }` so API keys are never passed into agent tool runtimes.\n- **Agent Skill Guidelines (`skill/SKILL.md`)**:\n  - Instructions on interacting with PagerDuty tools safely (incidents, services, on-call schedules, incident notes).\n  - Enforces read-first safe defaults, narrow query scoping to protect rate limits, redaction of sensitive incident payloads, and prompt injection defense.\n- **Console Desktop Assets**:\n  - Added official brand icon (`pagerduty.svg`), attribution in `NOTICE.md`, and brand accent theme styling in `connection-icon.tsx`.\n- **Tests**:\n  - Updated `test_loader.py` asserting catalog loading, fields, region choices, identity headers, and token lifetimes for PagerDuty.\n  - Updated `test_registry.py`, `test_connection_catalog.py`, and `test_workspace_services.py` for enabled service catalog integrity across the gateway and broker adapters.\n\n### Testing\n\n```bash\nuv run pytest tests/switch_core/connections/test_loader.py -k \"pagerduty\"\nuv run pytest tests/switch_core/connections/test_registry.py -k \"github_gets_its_adapter or key_service\"\nuv run ruff check switch_core tests\nuv run ruff format --check switch_core tests\n```\n\n#FliptheSwitch\n",
